---
source: src/main.rs
expression: "render_help_snapshot(&[\"tunnel\"])"
---
Expose a local HTTP server on a public Hooklistener URL

Usage: hooklistener tunnel [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  prepare  Validate authentication, schema compatibility, and the activation plan without connecting
  start    Prepare and activate a relay (the default when no subcommand is given)
  list     List tunnel sessions
  status   Show a tunnel session
  events   List lifecycle events, optionally following new ones
  capture  Show a redacted capture
  attempt  Show a delivery attempt
  stop     Stop a tunnel session, even if its CLI process is gone
  detach   Detach the current owner and keep the route for recovery
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -p, --port <PORT>         Local port to forward requests to [default: 3000]
      --host <HOST>         Local host to forward to [default: localhost]
  -o, --org <ORG_ID>        Organization ID (overrides the configured default)
  -s, --slug <SLUG>         Static tunnel slug to attach (from `static-tunnel create`)
      --allow-non-loopback  Allow a host that resolves outside loopback
      --no-replay-buffered  Do not replay requests buffered while the tunnel was offline
  -h, --help                Print help

Global options:
      --json               Output supported command responses or event streams as JSON
      --color <COLOR>      Styling policy for human output [default: auto] [possible values: auto,
                           always, never]
      --yes                Confirm destructive commands without an interactive prompt
      --log-level <LEVEL>  Log level [default: info] [possible values: trace, debug, info, warn,
                           error]
      --log-dir <DIR>      Directory for log files
      --log-stdout         Also write logs to stdout

TARGET FLAGS:
  Flags given before a subcommand set defaults; the same flag on the subcommand overrides them.
  hooklistener tunnel --port 3000          same as: hooklistener tunnel start --port 3000
